    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "1903\n1928\nCommem\nthe\nAnniversaru\nSheng,\nț he\nfirst\nairplane\nflight\nWright\nBrothers\nMax\nMiller\nCurtiss\nLangley\nChanute\nTN admiration and deepest respect\nfor those who daringly and hon-\norably aided science and history.\nI wish on this day which commem-\norates the 25th anniversary since\nthe birth of the first successfal\nFlying machine to offer my whole-\nhearted CONGRATULATIONS.\nByrd\nChamberlain\n\u0026 Levine\nAlcock \u0026\nBrown\nSantos\nDumont\nMaughan\nBurgess\nForman\nBleriot\nChavez\nAMERICA\nGAVE WINGS\nTHE WORLD\nDEC. 17\n1903\nLowell H.\nSmith\nLindbergh\nMaitland\nVon Konnefeld\nFitzmaurice\nHawker\nEckner\nCAPT. B. B. LIPSNER\nTHE\n(Former Regular Army Captain-Aviation Section Signal Corps)\nFIRST\nSUPERINTENDENT\nAIR- MAIL\nRODTURICDOTPCR\nBLAZE THE AIR-MAIL\n© 1928\nDE\nIDEC\n17\n1928\nAUGUSTA\nINTERNATIONAL CIVIL AERONAUTICS\nCONFERENCE\nVIA AIR MAIL\nAviationé-Iminrmante\nANNIVERSARY\nGHT\nWRIGHT BROS-\nĐEC.17,1903:\n127 N. Dearhorn Street\nSuite 1311-1G\nChiragn, Illinuis",
